<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ruaidri Ua Conchobair</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1116–1198</span> · Also known as Rory O'Connor</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ruaidri Ua Conchobair was king of Connacht and the last high king of Ireland, recognised from 1166. The Anglo-Norman invasion that followed undermined his position, and by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-windsor-1175">Treaty of Windsor</a> in 1175 he accepted Henry II's overlordship. He later retired to the abbey of Cong, where he died.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ruaidri-ua-conchobair.jpg" alt="Ruaidri Ua Conchobair" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: ClintMalpaso · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rory_O%27Connor_Stone_Carving.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
